(12. An Ode to Links) Tj
T*
(Source: Jim Nielsen?s Blog | Published: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:00:00 GMT) Tj
T*
(Link: https://blog.jim-nielsen.com/2026/ode-to-links/) Tj
T*
(A URL is a technical thing: a hostname, a path, a port, an origin, some query parameters, etc.) Tj
T*
(But a link is a cultural thing: an invitation, a citation, a gift, a shortcut, a connection.) Tj
T*
(All from a simple idea: here?s a thing that points to another thing, off you go! We?ve built an) Tj
T*
(entire culture around links. Just look at the language we use for them: ?Drop me a link.? ?Send) Tj
T*
(me the link.? ?Got a link?? ?Link in bio.? ?Link in the description.? ?Here?s the link.? ?Don?t) Tj
T*
(click that link.? ?Sorry, wrong link.? Or even just, ?Link?? Our language spans the spectrum of) Tj
T*
(meaning, from one end to the other: We save links. We lose links. We share links. We hide) Tj
T*
(links. We send links. We receive links. We collect links. We discard links. We open links. We) Tj
T*
(close links. We add links. We remove links. We make links. We break links. We shorten links. We) Tj
T*
(expand links. We follow links. We ignore links. We click links. We don?t click links. We link) Tj
T*
(in. We link out. We make links. Links make the web. The web makes Us. Reply via: Email ∑) Tj
T*
(Mastodon ∑ Bluesky) Tj
